course: dictionary
lesson: 2314
title: One word, three meanings: cropper
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cropper is a noun, and its meaning depends on the words around it. The most common use is the phrase «came a cropper», which means to fall over badly or to fail badly. «He came a cropper on his bike.» The clue is the bike: a fall or a crash fits well here.
explain: Cropper also has a gardening meaning. A «heavy cropper» is a plant that gives a lot of fruit. A «good cropper» is a plant that produces a lot. If the sentence is about apples, tomatoes or plants, think of this meaning.
explain: In US history, a cropper can be a sharecropper: a farmer who works land and pays the owner with part of the crop. Ask yourself what the sentence is about. Falls and failures, plants, or farms? Then test your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Cropper is a noun.
fact: «Came a cropper» means to fall over badly, or to fail badly.
fact: «Heavy cropper» means a plant that gives lots of fruit.
fact: «Sharecropper» (US, history) means a farmer who works land and pays the owner with part of the crop.
fact: «Came a cropper» is informal, and it is mostly heard in British, Irish, Australian and New Zealand talk.
exercise: «He came a cropper on his bike.» What does came a cropper mean here? | Rode past the park | Bought a new bike | *Fell over badly | Won the race
exercise: A gardener says her tomato plant is a heavy cropper. What does that mean? | It needs no water at all | It is very tall and thin | It has died | *It gives lots of fruit
exercise: In US history, a sharecropper was a farmer who | Sold shoes at the market | *Worked land and paid the owner with part of the crop | Owned a large castle | Ran the post office
test: «Her plan came a cropper when the bridge was closed.» What does this suggest? | Her plan was finished early | The bridge was painted bright red | Her plan was a huge success | *Her plan failed badly
test: Ben's apple tree gives hundreds of apples every autumn. Which phrase fits best? | sharecropper | cropper's cap | come a cropper | *a heavy cropper
exam: Cropper can mean a fall, a plant or a farmer. What is the best way to know which meaning is right? | Ask only someone who lives in another country | Guess at random and hope for the best | *Read the words around it and check which meaning fits the sentence | Always pick the first meaning you see in the dictionary
